    seoTitle: "Turning Social Media Followers into Sales",
    metaDescription:
      "Plenty of likes but few sales? How Kenyan businesses turn social media followers into enquiries and paying customers, with steps to try this month.",
    date: "February 2025",
    readMinutes: 9,
    excerpt: "You have 50,000 followers. Your posts get hundreds of likes. People comment, share, and tag their friends. And yet, your social media presence isn't generating the sales your business…",
    ctaTitle: "Want social media that actually drives sales?",
    ctaBody: "We design conversion-focused social strategies that turn audiences into customers.",
    image: "/brand/blog/from-followers-to-revenue.jpg",
    body: `<p>You have 50,000 followers. Your posts get hundreds of likes. People comment, share, and tag their friends. And yet, your social media presence isn't generating the sales your business needs. If this sounds familiar, the problem isn't your content — it's your conversion architecture. And the good news is, it's entirely fixable.</p><h2>The Vanity Metrics Trap</h2><p>Most social media reporting focuses on reach, impressions, follower growth, and engagement rate. These are useful signals, but they're not business outcomes. A post that reaches 100,000 people and generates zero purchase intent has performed worse for your business than a post that reaches 5,000 highly qualified prospects and drives 200 website visits.</p><p>The question to always be asking is not "how many people saw this?" but "how many people who saw this took the next step toward becoming a customer?"</p><h2>The Social Conversion Funnel</h2><ul><li><strong>Awareness content:</strong> Broad-reach content that introduces people to your brand — entertaining, educational, or emotionally resonant enough to stop the scroll and earn a follow.</li><li><strong>Consideration content:</strong> Content that speaks to people who already know you — demonstrating expertise, sharing proof, and answering the objections that prevent people from taking the next step.</li><li><strong>Conversion content:</strong> Direct offers, testimonials, case studies, and clear CTAs — content specifically designed to move warm audiences to a purchase or enquiry decision.</li><li><strong>Retention content:</strong> Content that keeps existing customers engaged, turns them into advocates, and drives repeat purchase and referral behaviour.</li></ul><h2>The Technical Side of Social Conversion</h2><blockquote><p>Your Instagram bio is a landing page. Treat it like one — one clear offer, one clear link, one clear reason to click.</p></blockquote><p>The most commonly overlooked conversion opportunities: a well-optimised link-in-bio page with clear paths for different audience intents, story CTAs that go to specific landing pages, and DM automation funnels that capture lead information conversationally at scale.</p><h2>Attribution: Knowing What's Actually Working</h2><p>UTM parameters on every link, Meta pixel on your website, and regular correlation analysis between content cadence and website traffic or sales will tell you more than most businesses ever know about which content is actually driving revenue. Start measuring the things that matter — not how many people liked your posts, but how many clicked through, signed up, purchased.</p>`,
